{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MVWJGAFRiyjyvJ8tMJ1mxJ","type":"tool_result","content":"Todos have been modified successfully. Ensure that you continue to use the todo list to track your progress. Please proceed with the current tasks if applicable"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cd9f14b9-5260-4636-ab39-a271be4bf43b","uuid":"848d6b30-2131-4a86-b8bd-f7136b14a3cf","timestamp":"2026-04-10T18:30:48.233Z","tool_use_result":{"oldTodos":[{"content":"Run before measurements (APC 0, 100, 300)","status":"completed","activeForm":"Running before measurements"},{"content":"Implement batched degenerate kernel (CUDA + Rust)","status":"completed","activeForm":"Implementing batched degenerate kernel"},{"content":"Build and verify correctness","status":"completed","activeForm":"Building and verifying correctness"},{"content":"Run after measurements (APC 0, 100, 300)","status":"in_progress","activeForm":"Running after measurements"},{"content":"Write report and update log","status":"pending","activeForm":"Writing report and updating log"},{"content":"Commit implementation and create tag","status":"pending","activeForm":"Committing implementation and creating tag"}],"newTodos":[{"content":"Run before measurements (APC 0, 100, 300)","status":"completed","activeForm":"Running before measurements"},{"content":"Implement batched degenerate kernel (CUDA + Rust)","status":"completed","activeForm":"Implementing batched degenerate kernel"},{"content":"Build and verify correctness","status":"completed","activeForm":"Building and verifying correctness"},{"content":"Run after measurements (APC 0, 100, 300)","status":"completed","activeForm":"Running after measurements"},{"content":"Write report and update log","status":"in_progress","activeForm":"Writing report and updating log"},{"content":"Commit implementation and create tag","status":"pending","activeForm":"Committing implementation and creating tag"}],"verificationNudgeNeeded":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01ERx4eriuFYEpRbLewjuTQi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015LAJrxKZXrxTuhDtDo5vTF","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-10-2145-batch-degenerate-stacked-reduction/report.md","content":"# Report: Batch Degenerate Stacked Reduction Kernel Launches\n\n## Description\n\nThe Stacked Reduction component of the GPU prover scales poorly with APC count: 113ms at APC 0 vs 312ms at APC 300 (2.76x increase), despite total work decreasing by >2x. The root cause is that `batch_sumcheck_poly_eval()` launches a separate CUDA kernel per \"window\" (one per trace matrix). For the degenerate case (`log_height < l_skip + round`), this produces ~10,348 single-block kernel launches at APC 300, each involving a fill_zero, H2D copy, kernel launch, and D2H sync. Nsight profiling confirmed ~70% of wall-clock time was CPU-side launch/sync overhead.\n\nThe optimization batches all degenerate windows into a single kernel launch per round, using one block per window, all atomically accumulating into a shared output buffer.\n\n## Implementation\n\n### Files changed\n\n| File | Change |\n|---|---|\n| `crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs` | Added `DegenerateWindowMeta` struct; restructured `batch_sumcheck_poly_eval` into 3 phases (classify, batched degenerate, per-window non-degenerate); removed unused `from_fn` import |\n| `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/stacked_reduction.cu` | Added `DegenerateWindowMeta` struct; added `stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate_batched_kernel` and its launcher |\n| `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/stacked_reduction.rs` | Added FFI extern declaration and safe wrapper for the batched launcher |\n| `crates/cuda-backend/src/error.rs` | Added `SumcheckMleRoundDegenerateBatched` error variant |\n\n### Key decisions\n\n- **Block size fixed at 256**: The original kernel used `min(window_len, 256)`. Fixing at 256 means some blocks have idle threads for small windows, but this is negligible (~3.9us avg GPU time per window) and avoids per-window block size tuning.\n- **Per-window metadata via device buffer**: A `DegenerateWindowMeta` struct (48 bytes) carries per-window parameters (col_offset, eq_ub_offset, window_len, eq_r, k_rot_r). At APC 300, this is ~10K * 48B = ~480KB, negligible.\n- **Concatenated eq_ub upload**: All degenerate windows' eq_ub values are gathered into one host Vec and uploaded in a single H2D copy, with per-window offsets in the metadata.\n\n### Deviations from plan\n\nNone. The implementation followed the plan exactly.\n\n## Results\n\n### Stacked Reduction (ms)\n\n| Config | Baseline | Before Task | After Task | vs Baseline | vs Before |\n|--------|----------|-------------|------------|-------------|-----------|\n| APC 0   | 113 | 113 | 101 | -12ms (1.12x lower) | -12ms (1.12x lower) |\n| APC 100 | 201 | 203 | 127 | -74ms (1.58x lower) | -76ms (1.60x lower) |\n| APC 300 | 308 | 312 | 147 | -161ms (2.10x lower) | -165ms (2.12x lower) |\n\n### STARK excl trace (ms)\n\n| Config | Baseline | Before Task | After Task | vs Baseline | vs Before |\n|--------|----------|-------------|------------|-------------|-----------|\n| APC 0   | 2149 | 2178 | 2147 | -2ms (1.00x lower) | -31ms (1.01x lower) |\n| APC 100 | 2159 | 2080 | 2006 | -153ms (1.08x lower) | -74ms (1.04x lower) |\n| APC 300 | 2478 | 2370 | 2195 | -283ms (1.13x lower) | -175ms (1.08x lower) |\n\n### Scaling ratio (APC 300 / APC 0)\n\n| Metric | Baseline | Before Task | After Task |\n|--------|----------|-------------|------------|\n| Stacked Reduction | 2.73x | 2.76x | 1.46x |\n| STARK excl trace | 1.153x | 1.088x | 1.022x |\n\n### Correctness\n\n- All 94 `openvm-cuda-backend` tests pass\n- Proof verification succeeds for all APC configs (0, 100, 300)\n- GPU memory unchanged (peak within 1% of before)\n\n## Assessment\n\nThis optimization achieved all success criteria:\n\n1. **Primary**: Stacked Reduction APC 300 dropped from 312ms to 147ms (53% reduction, target was >50%). **Met.**\n2. **Secondary**: STARK excl trace APC 300 dropped from 2478ms baseline to 2195ms (11.4% reduction, target was >10%). **Met.**\n3. **Scaling**: APC 300/APC 0 STARK excl trace ratio dropped from 1.153 (baseline) to 1.022 (target was <1.05). **Met.**\n4. **Correctness**: All tests pass. **Met.**\n\nThe combined effect of the two optimizations (Round 0 deferred sync + Stacked Reduction batching) brought STARK excl trace APC 300 from 2478ms to 2195ms, a cumulative 283ms (11.4%) improvement. The scaling ratio improved from 1.153 to 1.022, meaning APC 300 now performs nearly on par with APC 0 for STARK computation.\n\nThe Stacked Reduction scaling ratio (APC 300 / APC 0) improved dramatically from 2.73x to 1.46x. The remaining gap (1.46x vs ideal 1.0x) is likely from non-degenerate windows (which still have per-window launches) and residual overhead from the larger number of non-degenerate windows at higher APC counts.\n\n## Future Work\n\n- **Batch non-degenerate stacked reduction kernels**: The non-degenerate path still uses per-window launches. At APC 300, these are fewer in number and have larger grids, but batching them could save another 30-50ms.\n- **Rayon parallelization of Round 0 Phase 2**: The CPU-side processing in Round 0 could be parallelized across traces for ~30-50ms savings at APC 300.\n- **Multi-stream pipelining**: The degenerate and non-degenerate phases could potentially overlap on separate CUDA streams, though the benefit may be limited since the non-degenerate kernels are already larger.\n- **Persistent metadata buffer**: Currently `d_metas` is allocated/freed each round. A persistent buffer sized to the max degenerate window count could save allocation overhead, though this is likely negligible.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":312,"cache_read_input_tokens":88436,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":312},"output_tokens":67,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cd9f14b9-5260-4636-ab39-a271be4bf43b","uuid":"46c9009e-fc55-4d13-a3e2-1896290f1044"}
